        "original_id": "b899fd21-fcb6-594f-99eb-552bc6fba921",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eve Beglarian, Zach Bogosian, Jack Roslovic, Evander Kane, Tyler Myers, Drew Stafford, Joel Armia, Brendan Lemieux\n- Products: Overstepping\n- Organizations: Winnipeg Jets, Buffalo Sabres\n- Places: Ann Arbor, Michigan, United States\n- Topics: Armenian descent, music, NHL trades\n\nFacts:\n- Eve Beglarian was born in Ann Arbor, Michigan, United States, on July 22, 1958.\n- Eve Beglarian is a contemporary American composer, performer, and audio producer of Armenian descent.\n- Overstepping is the 1998 debut album by avant-garde composer Eve Beglarian.\n- Zachary M. Bogosian is also known as Zach Bogosian.\n- The Winnipeg Jets traded Evander Kane and Zach Bogosian to the Buffalo Sabres in exchange for Tyler Myers, Drew Stafford, Joel Armia, and Brendan Lemieux.\n- The draft pick acquired by the Winnipeg Jets in that trade was later associated with Jack Roslovic.",
